    "start": {
      "id": "start",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "Let's learn missing values and basic equation rearrangement.\n\nThis lesson uses the methods and question patterns from the Simplification chapter.\n\nWe will keep each step small: understand one rule, see it with numbers, then try a similar question.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "concept_1"
        }
      ]
    },
    "concept_1": {
      "id": "concept_1",
      "type": "CONTENT",
      "content": {
        "text": "A question mark is just an unknown number. Replace it by x, simplify the known part, then isolate x.\n\nExample:\n850 + x/10 = 900\nFirst x/10 = 50, so x = 500.\n\nOne unknown becomes much easier when the rest of the expression is reduced first.",
        "avatarPersona": "TUTOR"
      },
      "transitions": [
        {
          "targetNodeId": "q_1"
        }
      ]
    },
